                  "componentType": "textMeshPro",
                  "text": "Adenine (A) - Thymine (T) : 2 H-Bonds\\nGuanine (G) - Cytosine (C) : 3 H-Bonds",
                  "fontSize": 30
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Highlight the specific base pairs inside the helix and their hydrogen bonds",
          "narration": "Projecting inward are the nitrogenous bases. They pair strictly across the helix: Adenine always pairs with Thymine via two hydrogen bonds, and Guanine pairs with Cytosine via three hydrogen bonds. This complementary base-pairing is the key to genetic information storage."
        },
