            },
            {
              "target": "threePrimeLabel",
              "enabled": true
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Stop rotation to clearly point out the 5' and 3' ends of the antiparallel strands",
          "narration": "Look closely at the ends of the strands. Because of the asymmetrical structure of the sugar molecules in the backbone, the strands have a directionality. One strand runs 5 prime to 3 prime, while the opposite strand runs 3 prime to 5 prime. We call this an antiparallel orientation."
        }
